# Debugging the UI with XamlMcp

The `xamlmcp` MCP server (registered in `.cursor/mcp.json`) can attach to a
*running, Debug-build* instance of `PickMeWhatToListen.Wpf` and inspect/drive
its visual tree — prefer this over asking the user to describe the screen or
guessing at layout from XAML alone when debugging a UI issue.

- Full details, gotchas, and the exact attach wiring:
  [docs/references/xamlmcp-wpf.md](../../docs/references/xamlmcp-wpf.md).
- Quick loop: `dotnet run --project src/PickMeWhatToListen.Wpf` (Debug), then
  `list-apps` → `attach(instanceId)` → `tree`/`search`/`screenshot`/`input`.
- It only attaches in Debug builds and only while the process is alive —
  stop the running instance before rebuilding (locked `.exe`), and
  relaunch after any code change to pick it up again (no hot-reload of the
  agent itself).
- Node ids from `tree`/`search` are only valid for the `snapshotId` they
  came with; re-query after any mutating call.
